    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8f0e8fcf88b47efa75e76e7439151b1",
      "statement": "Where a sanctions-driven hold is dispositioned as an OFAC block, HMS enters its BLOCKED state, funds are moved to a blocked account, and the block is reported to OFAC within 10 business days (31 CFR 501.603); sanctions rejects carry a parallel reporting obligation under 31 CFR 501.604, both executed by Sanctions Operations rather than by SanctionScreen or engineering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L36-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39535041c8cc2d99b66c088d86e7324695c08d525da6b98bf32b3a4284a9d38d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L99-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9135e432b811788277f8bdc8d15d86947c3cc5727afc4bada09f8fb3ea4ca958:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1afac348e5514ba28b72536a45ea50fe",
      "statement": "POL-FCC-014 mandates that sanctions blocks and rejects be communicated only by Sanctions Operations per procedure, never by any client-facing channel, API, or notification, and Appendix C prohibits client-facing use of terms such as 'sanctions', 'OFAC', 'watch list', and 'screening hit'; this is stricter than the general tier R/G indistinguishability rule that otherwise applies to restricted holds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pol-fcc-014-v3.2-customer-communication-of-payment-status-holds-and-exceptions-standard.md#L63-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9696a0832d08702f2b972f4628bcc8103f5bcd96f3847b5e9e415cf4c1bd7487:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4220769ce5444a40875ce1c79e4674f2",
      "statement": "No client self-service resolution path exists for HRC-09 sanctions holds: the only production client-attestation flow (CTRL-PAY-031) is scoped exclusively to HRC-01, and the proposed client-facing hold-status facade (FCT-1893) was deprioritized in 2025-Q3 and was never built.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/prsp-hms-3.4-hold-management-service-design-and-reason-taxonomy-restricted.md#L88-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b77b6b57f287ea1274fc6b4756c91d59a706915cbedad5977e23ec9bae984e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c83b2a36af2b4bdfbb73287115731252",
      "statement": "The source corpus contains no dedicated SanctionScreen design document, API catalog, or match-logic specification; SanctionScreen's documented behavior is derived entirely from its role in PPH's screening stage, HMS's hold-creation handoff, and POL-FCC-014's sanctions-communication rules.",
